      "created_at": "2022-10-25T16:52:13Z",
      "updated_at": "2022-10-25T16:52:13Z",
      "body": "\"_Soft delete always_\" ? I do not think that is needed, even with GDPR. \r\n\r\nTechnically for GDPR compatibility a user can request data removal and our current system covers regulation requirements pretty well;\r\n\r\n1. User has \"non personal data\" (pireps, acars records, finance records etc) in the system : \r\n   *Remove personal data (change name, mail, password, ivao/vatsim id etc) , make non personal data non-identifiable / trackable*\r\n2. User has NO \"non personal data\" in the system : \r\n    *Delete the user directly*\r\n\r\nFor scenario 2 we do not need to \"soft delete\", we just need to delete the record that's it.\r\n\r\nIn short, **just click the delete button from admin area** v7 will take care the rest.\r\n(_or if needed we can allow the users to delete themselves from user profile directly_)\r\n\r\nSo again, I really and honestly do not understand the feature request or the logic behind it. @arv187 is technically requesting the same thing we already have but wants it to have with more clicks ? Either he is unaware of the current system or wanting something different like;\r\n\r\n`... In any case, it could be useful if a pilot wants to go back and recover all his progress after asking for his data to be deleted.`\r\n\r\nSecond part of this request is not possible and should not be possible. \r\n\r\nOnce you request a GDPR removal **there is no way of going back** . It is a removal decision and it is a serious act, not something you change two days later. So if the person wants to join back he/she needs to start from the beginning like every other **new member**.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
