      "created_at": "2022-10-25T17:59:46Z",
      "updated_at": "2022-10-25T18:19:01Z",
      "body": "So it's implemented, great.\r\nMainly, the issue came from not understanding the difference between the option \"state = deleted\" and using the delete user \"X\" button.\r\n\r\nI thought that deleting user completely deletes everything, pireps, stats and could have unwanted behaviour that could cause system errors.\r\n\r\nAbout going back, it is possible, you delete those personal data. If he comes back, for the initials or the pilot ID, you could edit by hand the email address that the person gives you, so that he could ask the system for a new password \"because he forgot it\".\r\n\r\nBut you are right, if he leaves and asks to delete his data (name and email), he should think twice before leaving and losing his achievements and stats.\r\n\r\nSo what is the function of changing the \"state\" to \"deleted\" when editing a user?\r\n\r\nP.S: Ok, I think I got it, even if you can put the deleted status in the pilot's profile by hand, it does that automatically when you delete the user with the red button, right? I didn't get to check it for fear of deleting the one user who left. Sorry xD\r\n\r\nYou can close this issue.",
